Subject: Clear the operand-stack slot before a helper consumes the value it names

What this does
  Stores undefined into the operand-stack slot at the moment a slow-path helper
  moves the operand's reference into a C local, in the twelve helpers that read
  their operands from sp[-2] and sp[-1].

Why we need it
  Those helpers hand the operand to a conversion that consumes the reference and
  then convert the other operand, which can run user code. From the first call
  until the result is stored, the slot names a value the helper no longer owns,
  so anything that inspects the operand stack during that window reads a stale
  reference.

What it adds
  Nine two-operand sites clear both slots and three single-operand sites clear
  the one, at the point where the reference moves rather than after the
  conversion returns. The value the helper computes, the reference it releases on
  each failure path and every observable result are unchanged. No opcode is added
  or retired and BC_VERSION is unchanged.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
